1mhj|v|To carry or bring (something) forward, or before one; hence, to bring for consideration, acceptance, judgment, etc.; to offer; to present; to proffer; to address; -- said especially of a request, prayer, petition, claim, charge, etc. ; To go before, or be before, in estimation; to outrank; to surpass. ; To cause to go before; hence, to advance before others, as to an office or dignity; to raise; to exalt; to promote; as, to prefer an officer to the rank of general. ; To set above or before something else in estimation, favor, or liking; to regard or honor before another; to hold in greater favor; to choose rather; -- often followed by to, before, or above.	o:3g6,21,10;1xtc,13,8;20bd,4,4~3g6,21,10;1xtc,13,8;20bd,4,4	s:nm4,45,4;1irv,25,21;1n1n,21,5;20bd,14,8~1irv,25,21;20bd,14,8;1n1n,21,5;nm4,45,4	d:28tq,67,3;1j8t,51,15;26jb,33,5;v7j,26,5;28h2,24,8;y1,18,7;1cca,17,13;1n43,14,6;176l,14,4;1zq9,12,6;ydm,8,6;1psw,5,4~1j8t,51,15;1cca,17,13;28h2,24,8;y1,18,7;1zq9,12,6;1n43,14,6;ydm,8,6;26jb,33,5;v7j,26,5;1psw,5,4;176l,14,4;28tq,67,3
