1mx4|n|The sum or amount of money at which a thing is valued, or the value which a seller sets on his goods in market; that for which something is bought or sold, or offered for sale; equivalent in money or other means of exchange; current value or rate paid or demanded in market or in barter; cost. ; Value; estimation; excellence; worth. ; Reward; recompense; as, the price of industry.	a:1rmt,100,3;1jx,73,2;1pu8,58,15;17zd,45,11;5ts,44,3;yp2,41,10;caf,41,3;17zi,40,7;yoz,34,9;1thb,22,10;1x8n,20,3;hp5,20,3;w53,1,3~1pu8,58,15;17zd,45,11;yp2,41,10;1thb,22,10;yoz,34,9;17zi,40,7;caf,41,3;1rmt,100,3;1x8n,20,3;w53,1,3;hp5,20,3;5ts,44,3;1jx,73,2	N:1piv,68,20;22f7,48,18;khv,39,7;1l91,35,16;22fi,33,3;1l9d,27,3~1piv,68,20;22f7,48,18;1l91,35,16;khv,39,7;1l9d,27,3;22fi,33,3
